{
  "project_name": "codemonkey",
  "programming_languages": ["Python"],
  "summary": "codemonkey is a scriptable, headless coding-agent CLI (Python 3.11 with Typer, Rich, and httpx, no LLM SDKs) for OpenAI-style and Anthropic-style endpoints, designed to run unattended against a local llama.cpp server or any OpenAI-compatible API. It offers an interactive REPL plus non-interactive commands (exec, review, sessions, journal, undo, eval) with JSONL event streams, structured output via JSON schema, session resume, checkpoints/undo, an execution journal, rule-based tool permissions, multi-provider YAML/.env configuration, and a pluggable strategy architecture for compaction, memory, and session state, so other agents and CI pipelines can drive it to write code by request with machine-readable output."
